<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Pass the carrier role of a vocoder from one deck to the other so a voice carries across the change."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "vocoder handoff"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-vocoder-handoff> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Repeat ever shorter slices of the playing audio to build tension."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-loop-roll> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "loop roll"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PerformMove> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-loop-roll> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-echo-out> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Feed the outgoing deck into a delay and cut the dry signal, leaving the echoes to trail away."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-echo-out> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/move-echo-out> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "echo out"@en .
