<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/normal-form> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A choice of one representative for every set of programs the symmetric monoidal laws make equal. Because the canonical text is such a representative, equal processes get equal CIDs."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/normal-form> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/normal-form> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "normal form modulo the SMC laws"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/normal-form> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/normal-form> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/open-net-cospan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#hasPort> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/open-net-cospan> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A net with named ports at its boundary, as a cospan of sets of places. Imports and macro definitions are read this way: they are glued to the rest of a program by identifying ports."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/open-net-cospan> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/open-net-cospan> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "open net (cospan)"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/open-net-cospan> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/open-net-cospan> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/pattern-endofunctor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Pattern as a functor from notes to notes: a function on single notes lifts to a function on patterns of them, and lifting respects composition and identity."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/pattern-endofunctor> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/pattern-endofunctor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Pattern endofunctor"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/pattern-endofunctor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/pattern-endofunctor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The pattern transforms, each taking a pattern to a pattern, closed under doing one after another, with doing nothing as the identity."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "endomorphism monoid"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/endomorphism-monoid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The section with no lines. Arranging it before or after any section leaves that section unchanged."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/empty-section-identity> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "empty section (identity)"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/empty-section-identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/sequential-composition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Arrangement: one section followed by the next, the output marking of the first being the input of the second. Associative."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/sequential-composition> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/sequential-composition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "sequential composition"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/sequential-composition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/sequential-composition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/silence-unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The part that plays nothing. Stacking it with any part gives that same part back."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/silence-unit> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/silence-unit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "silence (monoidal unit)"@en .
