<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Stacking parts side by side: two parts played together make one part whose net is the disjoint union of the two. Written with the tensor sign. Associative and symmetric: the order parts are listed in does not change what plays."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/monoidal-product> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "monoidal product"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/monoidal-product> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/free-smc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/note-transition> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/free-smc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-place> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/free-smc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The category whose objects are multisets of places and whose morphisms are generated by the net's transitions. A deck's net is read as this category: what the deck can do is exactly what the category's morphisms can do."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/free-smc> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/free-smc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "free symmetric monoidal category on a net"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/free-smc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CategoricalConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/free-smc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#liftedThrough> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#liftedThrough> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The functor a transform on single notes is lifted through to act on whole patterns."@en .
