<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#programCid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The program's ProgramCID, as its text form."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#programCid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "program CID"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#programCid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#programCid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Program> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#programCid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#programCid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#NetCID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#modelCID> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#NetCID> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#NetCID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The content identifier of the Petri net one deck runs, in pflow's canonical net form. Two decks with equal nets have equal NetCIDs whatever program produced them."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#NetCID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "net CID"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#NetCID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#NetCID> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramCID> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramCID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The content identifier of a program's canonical text."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramCID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "program CID"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramCID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramCID> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A name derived from the bytes it names (a CID): the same content always has the same identifier."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "content identifier"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ContentId> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Deck> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "stable" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Deck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One playback channel of the DJ app. Each deck runs a Petri net compiled from a program."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Deck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "deck"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Deck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Deck> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CanonicalForm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The normal form of a btw program: whitespace, numbers, note spelling and comments are normalised, so two spellings of one program have one canonical text and therefore one CID."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "canonical form"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#CanonicalForm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#TimingWord> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#TimingWord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A phrase that says when a change happens: at a bar, on the next phrase, every N bars, for N bars, or as a ramp."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#TimingWord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "timing word"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#TimingWord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#TimingWord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArpTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArpTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A chord's notes played one after another across the step."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArpTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "arp term"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArpTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArpTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ChordTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Several notes sounded together on one step."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "chord term"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ChordTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclidTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclideanRhythm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclidTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclidTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "K hits spread evenly over N steps, as a Euclidean rhythm."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclidTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "euclid term"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclidTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclidTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#AlternationTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#AlternationTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Terms taken in turn, one per pass through the pattern."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#AlternationTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "alternation"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#AlternationTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#AlternationTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GroupTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GroupTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Several terms squeezed into the time of one step."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GroupTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "group"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GroupTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GroupTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RestTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A step that is silent."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "rest"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RestTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#HitTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#HitTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A step that sounds."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#HitTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "hit"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#HitTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#HitTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One element of a part's pattern."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pattern term"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PatternTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Ending> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Ending> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What happens when a program's last section finishes: it ends, or it loops back to the start."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Ending> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ending"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Ending> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Ending> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#DoLine> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#DoLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Runs one verb of the control language, so a program can reach any control the app has without a dedicated syntax for it."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#DoLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "do line"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#DoLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#DoLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ImportLine> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ImportLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Brings in another program by CID. Pinning by content identifier means the imported text can never change under the importer."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ImportLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "import line"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ImportLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ImportLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArrangeLine> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArrangeLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Orders section blocks in time. Read categorically, it is sequential composition."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArrangeLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "arrange line"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArrangeLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ArrangeLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionBlock> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named group of lines that plays as one section of the piece. Unrelated to ns:SongSection, which is a genre-level template slot; a section block is whatever the author wrote."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "section block"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionBlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MacroDefinition> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MacroDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A parameterised macro. It is total: a macro cannot call itself, directly or through others, so expansion always ends. Repetition is written repeat N."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MacroDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "def (macro definition)"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MacroDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MacroDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#LetLine> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#LetLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Binds a name to a value or pattern for use further down the program."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#LetLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "let line"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#LetLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#LetLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlLine> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A line that sets something about the deck rather than playing notes: tempo, key, a level."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "control line"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PartLine> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PartLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A line that names a part (drums, bass, lead) and gives it a pattern of terms to play."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PartLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "part line"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PartLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#PartLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One line of a btw program. The kind of line says what it declares."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "program line"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ProgramLine> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Program> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#PetriNet> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Program> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> "in-development" .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Program> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A piece written in btw, the bitwrap language: lines of text that compile to the Petri nets of a DJ deck. Identified by the CID of its canonical text."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Program> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "btw program"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Program> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Program> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Maturity of a term's subject in the apps: \"stable\" (shipped) or \"in-development\" (on an unmerged branch; the definition may change)."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "status"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#status> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlNet> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A control net is a linear workflow: its transitions fire once, in order."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlNet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#PetriNet> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A rhythm ring is a state machine in pflow's sense: every transition has one input place and one output place, and the net holds exactly one token."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#PetriNet> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/song-structure-net> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#ControlNet> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/song-structure-net> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A linear control net whose transitions mute and unmute tracks and activate slots at section boundaries, so the order of sections is the order of transitions firing."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/song-structure-net> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "song structure net"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/song-structure-net> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/song-structure-net> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A phrase answered by another phrase."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "call and response"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/call-and-response> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/tension-curve> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A rise and release of intensity across a section or song."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/tension-curve> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "tension curve"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/tension-curve> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/tension-curve> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/syncopation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Accents placed off the strong beats."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/syncopation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "syncopation"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/syncopation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/syncopation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ghost-note> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A very quiet drum hit between the main ones, felt more than heard."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ghost-note> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ghost note"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ghost-note> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ghost-note> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The share of steps that sound rather than rest."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "density"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/density> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/rotation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Shifting a rhythm's pulses by a number of steps without changing their spacing."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/rotation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "rotation"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/rotation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/rotation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A scale degree that belongs to the chord sounding now. Strong-beat melody notes are pulled to the nearest one."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "chord tone"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/chord-tone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A melody made by a chain in which the next scale degree depends on the current one and the position in the bar: strong beats land on the nearest chord tone, weak beats move by step or repeat. A density setting then turns the weakest-beat notes into rests, never the first step."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Markov melody"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/markov-melody> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EuclideanRhythm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A rhythm made by the Bjorklund algorithm. Many traditional patterns around the world are Euclidean rhythms. In the engine it becomes a rhythm ring with a note binding on each pulse step."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Euclidean rhythm"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/euclidean-rhythm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_rhythm> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The procedure that spreads K pulses over N steps as evenly as possible. Applied repeatedly, it merges the longer groups with the leftover shorter ones until at most one leftover remains."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Bjorklund algorithm"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/bjorklund> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-arc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#Arc> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-arc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An arc from a place to its transition, or from a transition to the next place; together they close the ring."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-arc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "step arc"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-arc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-arc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ring-marking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#Marking> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ring-marking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Where the token sits in each ring right now: the whole state of the sequencer. A track's marking resets to its initial marking at the loop point."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ring-marking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ring marking"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ring-marking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/ring-marking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#Token> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The single token that moves around a ring, one step per tick. Its position is the playhead."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "circulating token"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/circulating-token> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/note-transition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#Transition> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/note-transition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A ring transition that carries a MIDI binding. Firing it plays the note; a transition without a binding passes the token silently."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/note-transition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "note transition"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/note-transition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/note-transition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://ontology.pflow.xyz/ns#Place> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One of the N places in a rhythm or melody ring. Each place is one step of the pattern."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "step place"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-place> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/concept/step-place> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/wobble-bass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A bass whose filter is modulated at a steady rate, giving the dubstep wobble."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/rave-stab> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A short, hard chord stab."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/detuned-saw> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lead made of detuned sawtooth oscillators."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/drums-v8> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A drum kit used for the hardest, fastest genres."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/scream-lead> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A harsh, distorted lead."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/drums-breakbeat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A drum kit used for breakbeat patterns."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/reese> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A bass made of detuned, phasing sawtooth oscillators, a drum-and-bass staple."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/square-lead> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lead built on a square wave."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/fm-bell> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A bell tone made by frequency modulation."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/warm-pad> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A slow, soft sustained pad."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/drums-cr78> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A drum kit styled on the CR-78 rhythm machine."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/sub-bass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A low sine-like bass with almost no upper harmonics."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/vibes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A vibraphone sound."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/bass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A plain bass synth."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/electric-piano> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An electric-piano keys sound."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/drums> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The default electronic drum kit."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/acid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A resonant filtered sawtooth bass of the acid-house kind."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/bright-pluck> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A pluck with an open, bright filter."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/pluck> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A short, percussive plucked tone."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/instrument/supersaw> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A stack of detuned sawtooth oscillators: the wide, bright trance and EDM lead."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/outro> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The closing section: parts fall away."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/solo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A section featuring one melodic voice over the rhythm section."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/bridge> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A contrasting section away from the verse and chorus."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/breakdown> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A stripped-back section where the drums drop out and a melody carries."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/buildup> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Rising tension before a drop: snare and hi-hat density climb."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/drop> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The peak of an electronic track after a buildup: full arrangement at highest energy."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/chorus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The high-energy, full-arrangement section a song returns to."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/pre-chorus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A short lift into the chorus."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/verse> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A main body section carrying the groove with moderate energy."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/section/intro> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The opening: few parts playing, building attention."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/arp> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An arpeggio: chord tones played one after another."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/harmony> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Chordal accompaniment: pads, keys or stabs."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/melody> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The lead line."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/bass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The low line that carries the harmony's roots."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/clap> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A hand-clap sound doubling the snare."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/hihat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The hi-hat: keeps the subdivision."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/snare> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The snare drum: marks the backbeat."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/role/kick> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bass drum: marks the pulse."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/groove/bossa> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A syncopated ostinato alternating the root and the low fifth, the bossa nova bass figure."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/groove/walking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A steady quarter-note bass line that walks through the chord tones, independent of the kick."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/groove/breakbeat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bass plays about three eighths of the steps, evenly spread and randomly rotated, independent of the kick."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/groove/syncopated-pocket> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bass follows the kick and adds two off-beat hits, on steps 6 and 14 of a sixteen-step bar (3 and 7 of eight)."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/groove/sidechained> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bass plays wherever the kick does not, so the two never sound together."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/groove/offbeat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bass plays one step before each kick, in the gap the kick leaves."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/groove/four-on-floor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The bass plays exactly where the kick plays."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/scale/blues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The minor pentatonic scale plus the flattened fifth, the blue note."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/scale/minor-pentatonic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The five-note minor pentatonic scale."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/scale/pentatonic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The five-note major pentatonic scale: the major scale without its fourth and seventh."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/scale/harmonic-minor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Natural minor with a raised seventh degree."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/scale/phrygian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Minor with a lowered second degree: the third mode of the major scale. Dark and tense."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/scale/mixolydian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Major with a lowered seventh: the fifth mode of the major scale."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/scale/dorian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Minor with a raised sixth degree: the second mode of the major scale."@en .
