<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MelodyRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The same ring, with a note binding on every non-rest step: a melody, bass line or arpeggio written out as a cycle."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MelodyRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Melody ring"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MelodyRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineNet> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MelodyRing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "N places in a cycle, one token circulating, one transition per step; transitions at pulse positions carry a note binding, the rest are silent. Realises a Euclidean rhythm."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rhythm ring"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#EngineNet> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#RhythmRing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
