<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One numbered place in a song structure, filled by a section."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Section slot"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SectionSlot> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongStructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An ordered template of sections for one genre family and length class."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongStructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Song structure"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongStructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongStructure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named stretch of a song: intro, verse, drop and so on."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Song section"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#SongSection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Instrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named sound the synth engine can play."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Instrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Instrument"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Instrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Instrument> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#InstrumentRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The job a track does in the mix: kick, snare, hihat, clap, bass, melody, harmony, arp."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#InstrumentRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Instrument role"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#InstrumentRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#InstrumentRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Groove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "How the bass line locks to the drums."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Groove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Groove"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Groove> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Groove> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A set of pitch-class offsets in semitones from a root."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scale"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Scale> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GenreFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A group of genres that share song structures and section energy: edm, song, jazz, chill."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GenreFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genre family"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GenreFamily> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#GenreFamily> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Genre> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A style the sequencer can generate a whole track in. Each carries the defaults that make it recognisable: tempo, scale, drum rhythms, groove, feel."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Genre> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genre"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Genre> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#Genre> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Root of everything this ontology describes about music."@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Music concept"@en .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns#MusicConcept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.bitwrap.io/ns> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Genres a Petri-net beat sequencer can generate (tempo, scale, groove, Euclidean drum rhythms, instruments, chord progressions), the song structures and section profiles it arranges them into, and the engine concepts (rhythm rings, Markov melody, control nets) that realise them. Draft scope: DJ- and musician-facing."@en .
